/-! ## NaN: where the model differs from Rust

Lean's model has a single, positive NaN. In Rust, `f32::from_bits(0xFFC00000)` is a NaN with
the sign bit set: `to_bits` gives back `0xFFC00000` and `is_sign_negative` is `true`, and
`1.0f32.copysign(that NaN)` is `-1.0`. In the model all three use the canonical NaN instead. -/

example : (core.f32.to_bits (core.f32.from_bits 0xFFC00000#u32)).bv.toNat = 0x7FC00000 := by decide
example : core.f32.is_sign_negative (core.f32.from_bits 0xFFC00000#u32) = false := by decide
example : core.f32.copysign (Float32.ofBits 0x3F800000) (Float32.ofBits 0xFFC00000) =
    Float32.ofBits 0x3F800000 := by decide
example : (core.f64.to_bits (core.f64.from_bits 0x7FF0000000000001#u64)).bv.toNat =
    0x7FF8000000000000 := by decide
